=== AsyncDropChaining Sample ===
--- 1. Func auto-unwrap in sync context ---
  FetchAsync(test) executed
  lambdaResult=result-test
  type is string (not Task): True
--- 2. Func auto-unwrap computed ---
  computeResult=105
--- 3. Async functor scope-exit ---
  async functor produced Task, value will be: 42
  async functor scope-exit completed
--- 4. Recursive drop Task scope-exit ---
  Task<int> captured via async functor
  task scope-exit drop resolved
--- 5. Custom recursive drop ---
  DropChainBox created
  DropChainBox(boxed).Drop() called, yielding ResourceHandle
  ResourceHandle(boxed).Drop() called
  custom recursive drop completed
--- 6. Non-recursive drop baseline ---
  handle created
  ResourceHandle(baseline).Drop() called
  non-recursive drop done
--- 7. Explicit capture stops recursion ---
  DropChainBox(captured).Drop() called, yielding ResourceHandle
  DropChainBox dropped, inner handle captured
  ResourceHandle(captured).Drop() called
  explicit capture completed
=== AsyncDropChaining Done ===
